Author: Luke Curley <kixelated@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 25 12:36:46 2026 -0800

    fix(net): a lite-06 relay's rejoin asks upstream for the reader's own live join
    
    An idle copy resubscribing asked a lite-06 publisher from the newest group it
    cached even for a live join, which the publisher decodes as a join placed
    there (min 0). A retaining audio encoder sizes its replay by the join's reach,
    so it dropped all of its retention and the player rejoined across a gap.
    Lite-06 resolves an absent start within the max age, so only pre-06 wires
    still need the cached head.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

